@startuml
title v0001-executor-docker - Executor process state machine (MVP)

state "starting" as Starting
state "registering" as Registering
state "ready\n(polling Router, capacity available)" as Ready
state "busy\n(one or more task containers running)" as Busy
state "draining\n(SIGTERM, draining owned containers)" as Draining
state "stopped" as Stopped

[*] --> Starting : process init
Starting --> Registering : init complete\n(config read, image pulled)
Registering --> Ready : State Registry registration 2xx
Registering --> Stopped : registration/event append or\nstartup retries exhausted

Ready --> Busy : queued task accepted,\ncontainer started
Busy --> Ready : all task containers terminal
Busy --> Busy : one task container terminal,\nothers still running

Ready --> Draining : SIGTERM
Busy --> Draining : SIGTERM
Draining --> Stopped : drain complete OR\nOPENHANDS_DRAIN_TIMEOUT\nelapsed (force-kill)

Ready --> Stopped : fatal error
Busy --> Stopped : fatal error

Stopped --> [*]

note right of Registering
  Before accepting work,
  Executor removes any leftover containers
  from previous run via Docker labels.
end note

note right of Busy
  Individual container failure marks only
  that task failed and frees one slot.
  Other task containers continue.
end note

note right of Draining
  Stops polling Router.
  Tells every owned OpenHands container to drain.
  Appends terminal State Registry events.
  Stops and removes all owned containers.
end note

@enduml
